[1m[38;5;231mWhere should the persisted logs actually live?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mOn-device (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mBrowser: capped ring buffer in localStorage/IndexedDB with an export. Node: rotated file on disk. No backend [39m
     [38;5;246mneeded; adapter seam lets shipping drop in later.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Central collection
     [38;5;246mAdapters batch and POST to a collection endpoint you can query without the user. Requires a receiving service, [39m
     [38;5;246moffline buffering, retry, and a retention policy.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Both, tiered
     [38;5;246mAlways persist locally, ship warn/error centrally. Best debugging coverage, most moving parts. Worth it only if the
[39m     [38;5;246mendpoint already exists.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Node file only
     [38;5;246mPersist just the Node side to disk; browser keeps transient console output with levels and redaction.[39m
